package server

const mcpUnderstandingPolicy = "Use semantic overview for large diagrams: GET/PUT /diagrams/{diagramId}/overview with exact {baseVersion,overview:{version:1,enabled,grouping:auto|groups|tags|source,expanded:[]}}; GET /diagrams/{diagramId}/overview/projection?zoom=0.1 discovers stable view-only group IDs, status/count summaries, original-ID mappings and typed directed relation aggregates. Zoom is (0,10], with levels at 0.2/0.55/1.2. Update expanded with discovered overview-group IDs; never PATCH proxies as canonical nodes. Original objects and links remain intact. POST /diagrams/{diagramId}/questions is a read-only question accepting {startId,kind:downstream|upstream|path,targetId?,maxDepth?:1..64,edgeTypes?:[],includeHidden?:false,includeUncertain?:true,offset?:0,limit?:1..100}. It returns complete bounded-traversal counts, paged shortest modeled paths, source evidence and uncertainty/depth warnings. For path only, targetId is required. Directed paths exclude unarrowed associations. They do not prove runtime impact. GET /diagrams/{diagramId}/evidence?nodeId=UUID reads retained code/SQL/CSV metadata; add metricId and optional offset/disposition to request up to 100 original CSV measure-evidence rows. Original code/SQL scripts are not stored. Read-only POST /diagrams/{diagramId}/build-brief with {scope?:diagram|selected|csv-view,selectedIds?,instructions?} previews the full app brief, observed source facts, proposed screens/read API, acceptance criteria and unresolved decisions. It does not send to Lovable. GET/PUT /diagrams/{diagramId}/build-specification stores reviewed section additions and decision answers using {baseVersion,specification:{version:1,sections:{},answers:{}}}. Preview questions and build briefs do not mutate the graph and are allowed with Read only."

const mcpHistoryPolicy = "GET/POST /diagrams/{diagramId}/history lists versions or creates a named snapshot with exact {baseVersion,name}. GET/DELETE /diagrams/{diagramId}/history/{snapshotId} reads or removes a version; GET .../{snapshotId}/compare?to=current|snapshotUUID reviews semantic differences and modeled affected dependencies. POST .../{snapshotId}/restore with exact {baseVersion} atomically saves a pre-restore safety copy then restores IDs, layout, source versions, annotations and settings. Existing shared owner profiles stay current. Stale versions return 409 and failures preserve current work. Explicit named snapshots plus automatic pre-source-refresh/pre-restore checkpoints are separate from Undo/Redo; there is no snapshot on every autosave. History is local IndexedDB, portable in full workspace backups, limited to 50 versions per diagram/1,000 per workspace and 256MiB, with 32MiB per structural graph and deduplicated immutable source rows. Capacity errors do not silently evict named versions. Writes require accepted storage and Read + write."

const mcpStoryboardPolicy = "Storyboards coexist with numbered walkthroughs: GET/PUT /diagrams/{diagramId}/storyboard with exact {baseVersion,storyboard:{version:1,scenes:[{id,name,nodeIds,edgeIds,narration,seconds,transitionMs,view?}]}}. Up to 1,000 unique scene UUIDs and 100,000 total existing node/edge references; each scene has at least one node, name 1..200, narration<=12000, seconds 2..600 and transitionMs 0..10000. Edge endpoints participate in framing. Optional view is {mode:2d,viewport:{x,y,zoom}} or {mode:3d,camera:{position,target,up?}}; the authored view requires its matching current mode and Details (semantic overview off); mismatches return 422 before navigation or video export. Choose Details or omit view to auto-fit the same objects in either mode, including overview. Scenes temporarily highlight chosen content and use authored narration without changing node descriptions/layout. POST /presentation/open accepts optional diagramId and source:nodes|storyboard; default source is nodes. POST /presentation/seek with exact {index:zeroBasedExistingStep} previews paused. POST /presentation/video also accepts optional source; omission uses current player source. Scene movies use local English(default)/Swedish voice, subtitles, preload and collision-safe camera transitions with existing export limits. Playback state adds source,sceneId,nodeIds,edgeIds,title,narration; nodeId remains the first object and video nodeIndex means current step."
